{%- comment -%}
  PG Unlock Fix: the offer row's Add button sticks on "Adding..." when the click
  completes the ladder.

  THE BUG, precisely. pg-unlock's button never resets its own label on success.
  It sets "Adding...", posts the add, and leaves the reset to render(), which
  removes every .pg-unlock row and rebuilds from the current offers. render()
  is guarded so it does not thrash on its own 900ms tick:

      var key = offs.map(...).join('|');
      if (key === lastKey && c.querySelector('.pg-unlock')) return;

  and the success path invalidates that guard with

      lastKey = '';

  Those two collide in exactly one case. Adding the FREE 3rd orb completes the
  offer, so offers() returns an empty array, so `key` is the empty string --
  the same value the success path just wrote into lastKey as its "invalidate"
  sentinel. key === lastKey, a .pg-unlock row is still on screen, and render()
  returns early on that tick and every tick after it. The row it was about to
  remove stays forever, still reading "Adding...".

  So it is not intermittent: it is every click that takes a shopper to the last
  rung, and only those. A click that leaves an offer standing produces a
  different key and rebuilds normally.

  THE PROPER FIX is three characters in pg-unlock -- make the invalidation
  sentinel `null` instead of `''`, so it can never equal a real key, and reset
  the button in the success path rather than depending on a rebuild. That file
  is 17.8KB of money-critical BXGY logic and nothing here can be tested against
  a live storefront, so it is not being retyped through the API to change one
  token. This does the same job from outside.

  WHAT THIS DOES. It finishes what render() intended. Two and a half seconds
  after a click on the Add button, if the button still says "Adding...", the
  row is removed -- which is precisely the removal render() skipped. It is
  self-healing in both directions: a genuinely failed add says "Try again", not
  "Adding...", so it is left alone; and if the add was merely slow and the
  offer does in fact still stand, render() re-adds the row on its next tick,
  because its guard's second condition no longer finds a .pg-unlock element.

  No interval, no observer. One listener, one timeout per click.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgUnlockFix) return; window.pgUnlockFix = 1;

  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    var btn = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('.pg-unlock-add') : null;
    if (!btn) return;

    setTimeout(function(){
      /* "Try again" is pg-unlock reporting a real failure -- leave it be */
      if (!/adding/i.test(btn.textContent || '')) return;
      var row = btn.closest ? btn.closest('.pg-unlock') : null;
      if (row && row.parentNode) row.parentNode.removeChild(row);
    }, 2500);
  }, true);
})();
</script>
